  "concept": {
    "movement": "A low, deliberate bottom-cruise with a restrained armored forebody, continuous lateral caudal propulsion and small pectoral trim. Pursuit increases cadence and tail amplitude without vertical hopping.",
    "attack": "The pointed rostrum leads a low forward scooping body thrust. Load back briefly, lift the snout slightly through the forward surge, then recover without inventing a mouth hinge.",
    "death": "Propulsion fades as the long body drifts forward onto separate pelvic, central belly, chest and chin patches. Pectorals/pelvic fins, the two ventral blades, barbels and caudal panel release clear so the body is supported rather than suspended on appendages."
